<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<resources>
    <!-- The app's background, and the literal value of the bg custom property
         in frontend/src/app/globals.css and of layout.tsx's themeColor. It has
         to be a literal here: the window is painted by the OS before any web
         content exists, so it cannot read a CSS custom property. If that token
         changes, this changes with it, or the hand-off from the system splash
         to the WebView shows a seam.

         Named for the app rather than for one screen, because the window
         background is what shows through wherever the WebView has not drawn:
         behind the system bars, and for the moment between the window opening
         and the first web paint. Both #195 and #176 need exactly this value,
         and one name for it is what stops a fourth copy of #08070c appearing.

         Named without the leading hyphens of the CSS property on purpose. XML
         forbids a double hyphen anywhere inside a comment, and Android reports
         it from the resource merge rather than the parser, so the failure
         arrives as a line and column with no hint that a comment is the
         cause. -->
    <color name="appBackground">#08070c</color>
</resources>
